155 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 131 0 R
/T (The current model treats the nickel strip in isolation, which makes it a conservative baseline. Planned extensions include modeling conductive heat transfer into the connected cells, which act as heat sinks that would raise the true fusing current; simulating dynamic current profiles rather than a fixed current, to reflect real fault and load conditions; and modeling more complex strip geometries beyond the simplified shapes used here.)
/E (The current model treats the nickel strip in isolation, which makes it a conservative baseline. Planned extensions include modeling conductive heat transfer into the connected cells, which act as heat sinks that would raise the true fusing current; simulating dynamic current profiles rather than a fixed current, to reflect real fault and load conditions; and modeling more complex strip geometries beyond the simplified shapes used here.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
