179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 132 0 R
/T (The model is quite limited. The cell is treated as a single lumped thermal mass; heat generation is ohmic only, omitting entropic heat; current is derived from power using a fixed nominal voltage, ignoring voltage sag; and DCIR is a function of SOC only, without temperature dependence. The convective term and material properties are typical Li-ion assumptions rather than measured values.)
/E (The model is quite limited. The cell is treated as a single lumped thermal mass; heat generation is ohmic only, omitting entropic heat; current is derived from power using a fixed nominal voltage, ignoring voltage sag; and DCIR is a function of SOC only, without temperature dependence. The convective term and material properties are typical Li-ion assumptions rather than measured values.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 132 0 R
/T (Its strength is how little it needs. From only a DCIR curve, it produces useful data before a physical cell exists, or is even released, making it a practical screening tool for comparing candidate cells ahead of any bench testing. Measuring DCIR and temperature rise on a real cell to calibrate hA and confirm the model is the next step. )
/E (Its strength is how little it needs. From only a DCIR curve, it produces useful data before a physical cell exists, or is even released, making it a practical screening tool for comparing candidate cells ahead of any bench testing. Measuring DCIR and temperature rise on a real cell to calibrate hA and confirm the model is the next step. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
