269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/E (The objective of this project is to develop a precise and versatile light source for photographic film scanning. It uses five independent channels \(RGB, white, and infrared\) to deliver accurate color reproduction, uniform illumination, and added functions such as dust detection and IR transmission. With active temperature monitoring and efficient power control, the system supports high quality film digitization with greater flexibility.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/E (A Seeed Studio XIAO microcontroller controls the LightCore on a custom PCB. Power is managed with a two-stage system that steps 36V down to 5V through a buck converter and then to 3.3V with an LDO. Four AL8860WT LED drivers and a four-channel DAC provide precise current control of the RGBW channels, while a MOSFET circuit drives the infrared channel for dust removal and IR transmission. A temperature sensor actively monitors temperature to maintain stable functionality.  Together, these components form a reliable, high-precision platform for film scanning applications.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
